.\" robodr-replay(1). Source of truth: the USAGE text in
.\" crates/robodr-agent/src/bin/robodr-replay.rs. Keep the two in sync.
.TH ROBODR\-REPLAY 1 "2026-10-16" "RoboDR 0.1.0-alpha.1" "RoboDR Manual"
.SH NAME
robodr\-replay \- offline RoboDR decision chain (event \(-> deviation \(-> plan \(-> black box \(-> finding)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B robodr\-replay
.RB [ run ]
.B \-\-events
.I run.jsonl
.B \-\-profile
.I profile.json
.B \-\-policy
.I policy.json
.B \-\-blackbox
.I DIR
.B \-\-key\-file
.I FILE
.B \-\-robot\-id
.I ID
[\fIoptions\fR]
.PP
.B robodr\-replay verify
.B \-\-blackbox
.I DIR
.B \-\-key\-file
.I FILE
.RB [ \-\-robot\-id
.IR ID ]
.RB [ \-\-findings
.IR findings.jsonl ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B robodr\-replay
runs RobotEvent JSON Lines through the RoboDR decision chain offline, records
evidence in a fresh black box, writes findings, and verifies the result.
.B verify
re\-checks an existing black box directory (and, optionally, the evidence links
of a findings file) with the black\-box key.
.PP
A replay never acts:
.B \-\-log\-plans
only prints what would have been requested.
.SH RUN OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-events " run.jsonl\fR, " \-\-profile " profile.json\fR, " \-\-policy " policy.json"
Input events, model profile and response policy (required).
.TP
.BI \-\-blackbox " DIR"
Black\-box directory. Must be absent or empty (a replay starts a fresh chain).
.TP
.BI \-\-key\-file " FILE"
The black\-box key (required): a
.I robodr\-blackbox\-key/v1
file as written by
.BR "robodr\-blackbox keygen \-\-out" " \fIFILE\fR."
It is refused if it is a symlink or not a regular file, or if its mode gives
group or others any access (it must be
.BR "chmod 600" ).
Only hmac\-sha256 keys (at least 32 bytes) are accepted. The key id recorded in
the chain is the file's
.IR key_id .
Keys are never accepted on the command line (a command line is visible to
other users in
.IR /proc );
the former
.B \-\-key\-hex
and
.B \-\-key\-id
options were removed and are usage errors. HMAC is a placeholder
authenticator (see
.BR robodr\-blackbox (1)).
.TP
.BI \-\-robot\-id " ID"
Robot identity bound into the chain (required).
.TP
.BI \-\-out " findings.jsonl"
Findings file; default stdout. The summary goes to stderr.
.TP
.BI \-\-outcomes " outcomes.jsonl"
Write decision outcomes as JSON Lines.
.TP
.BI \-\-safety\-state " STATE"
idle | moving_slow | moving_fast | collaborative_human_nearby |
estop_active | safe_state_active | unknown (default unknown).
.TP
.BI \-\-control " autonomous|teleop|manual"
.TP
.BI \-\-phase " parked|transit|task|takeoff|landing|unknown"
.TP
.BI \-\-connectivity " connected|degraded|disconnected"
.TP
.B \-\-no\-operator
No operator present.
.TP
.BI \-\-site " NAME\fR, " \-\-model " NAME\fR, " \-\-profile\-version " V\fR, " \-\-boot\-id " ID"
Context and identity fields recorded with the evidence and findings.
Without
.BR \-\-model ,
the profile's model is used.
.TP
.BI \-\-start\-ms " EPOCH_MS\fR, " \-\-step\-ms " MS"
Synthetic clock: start time and step per event.
.TP
.B \-\-firewall
Enable the Motion Firewall.
.TP
.BI \-\-firewall\-allow " CHANNEL=GUID[,GUID...]"
Writers allowed on a channel (repeatable).
.TP
.BI \-\-firewall\-max\-angular " CHANNEL=RAD_PER_S"
The OEM's yaw\-rate bound for a Twist channel (repeatable).
.B \-\-firewall
needs it for every Twist channel of the profile (the profile has none).
.TP
.BR \-\-monitor " | " \-\-monitor\-config " \fIFILE\fR"
Enable the motion monitor with UGV defaults, or with a config file.
.TP
.BI \-\-feedback\-source " CHANNEL=SOURCE"
SOURCE: wheel_odometry | imu | joint_state | gnss | other (repeatable).
.TP
.B \-\-record\-all\-events
Record all events in the black box.
.TP
.BI \-\-partitions " N"
Kafka partition count recorded with the findings.
.TP
.B \-\-log\-plans
Print the response plans that would have been requested.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
OK and verified.
.TP
.B 1
Verification failed (black box or an evidence link).
.TP
.B 2
Usage, input, config, key file or I/O error, including an argument that is not
valid UTF\-8.
.TP
.B 3
.RB ( run
only) The evidence that was written verifies, but findings were lost: they
failed OCSF validation (for example a synthetic clock past what a finding can
carry) and were not written, so the findings output is incomplete. The summary
says
.BR "NOT VERIFIED" .
Exit 1 takes precedence over 3.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR robodr\-blackbox (1),
.BR robodr\-commission (1),
.BR robodr\-pulsard (8),
/usr/share/doc/robodr/OPERATIONS.md
